{#
  The site's search box (TASK-22): a plain GET form, so a search is a URL a
  reader can bookmark or share and the box needs no JavaScript.

  `layouts/search.njk` is the only thing that includes it (TASK-105): the box
  was in the footer of every page as well, and search is a menu item now —
  a `Search | /search/` line like any other — so the page about searching is
  where the box is.

  Expects nothing. `query`, when the page has one, goes back in the box, so the
  results page shows what was searched for. The label is read out rather than
  shown, because the button beside the box already says what it is for, and it
  wraps the field rather than naming an id, so the form can appear more than
  once on a page without two elements sharing one.
#}
<form class="search-form" role="search" action="{{ "/search/" | url }}" method="get">
  <label>
    <span class="screen-reader-text">Search this site</span>
    <input type="search" name="q" value="{{ query }}" placeholder="Search" maxlength="256" required>
  </label>
  <button type="submit">Search</button>
</form>
